# Don't fill this in by hand. From the repo root, run:
#
#   .venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts\generate_langfuse_env.py
#
# That generates a real docker/langfuse/.env with random secrets and an
# auto-provisioned org/project/admin user (no browser signup needed), and
# prints the LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY / LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY to copy into the
# project's own .env.
#
# This file just documents what ends up in docker/langfuse/.env:
#
# SALT                                          - random hex, used to hash user passwords
# ENCRYPTION_KEY                                - 32-byte hex (openssl rand -hex 32), encrypts stored API keys
# NEXTAUTH_SECRET                                - session signing secret for the Langfuse web app
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD                              - password for Langfuse's own Postgres (org/project/user data)
# DATABASE_URL                                   - full Postgres connection string, must embed POSTGRES_PASSWORD
# CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD                            - password for the ClickHouse trace/observation store
# REDIS_AUTH                                      - password for the Redis ingestion queue
# MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD                             - password for the MinIO (S3-compatible) blob store
# LANGFUSE_S3_*_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY (x3)             - must match MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD
# LANGFUSE_INIT_ORG_ID / ORG_NAME                  - auto-created organization
# LANGFUSE_INIT_PROJECT_ID / PROJECT_NAME          - auto-created project
# LANGFUSE_INIT_PROJECT_PUBLIC_KEY / SECRET_KEY    - the API keys the bot's .env needs
# LANGFUSE_INIT_USER_EMAIL / NAME / PASSWORD        - admin login for the Langfuse web UI at localhost:3000
